# Every run adds a section to this file at the same place, so two runs that worked side by side always conflicted in it and
# nowhere else (2026-09-19: three times in one morning). A union merge keeps both sides' lines. If two runs ever edit the same
# existing sentence, both versions are kept and a person tidies them.
packages/agent-orchestrator/docs/features.md merge=union

# Every CLAUDE.md is a list too, the root's and each package's: a run that learns something appends a lesson to one, so two runs side by
# side conflict in it though neither touched a line of the other's. A union merge keeps both lessons. The cost is the same as above: two
# edits of one existing line keep both versions, so whoever merges reads the merged file and tidies it (apps/web/test/e2e-merge.test.ts).
CLAUDE.md merge=union

# The e2e's list of its pages, a name a line (apps/web/test/e2e/pages.ts). Every run that adds a page adds its line at the end, so two runs
# side by side would conflict there as they did on the one array of pages this replaced. Union keeps both lines; the order of the lines means
# nothing, and the loader refuses the list and the page files when they differ (apps/web/test/e2e-merge.test.ts).
/apps/web/test/e2e/pages/NAMES merge=union

# The board's theme, written by the design system kit's generator from apps/web/DESIGN.md (`ds-theme`), and its route tree, written by
# TanStack Router's plugin from apps/web/src/routes: no person writes a line of either. Marked generated so that GitHub folds them in a
# diff and a quick run's `change.ts size`, which leaves out each file marked so, measures the change a person wrote and not its output.
/apps/web/theme/** linguist-generated
/apps/web/src/routeTree.gen.ts linguist-generated

# What is not ours: another project's files, vendored unchanged, and what a tool writes. Marked once here, in git's own words, so that
# GitHub folds them in a diff and every guard that leaves them unread asks git rather than keeping a list of its own (test-kit's `notOurs`,
# `git check-attr`). The design system kit and its skills (french-tech-homies/design-system), the skills vendored at the root and pinned in
# skills-lock.json, and npm's lockfile.
/apps/web/src/components/ui/ds/** linguist-vendored
/apps/web/.claude/** linguist-vendored
/.claude/skills/shadcn/** linguist-vendored
/.claude/skills/react-aria/** linguist-vendored
/.claude/skills/tsverify/** linguist-vendored
/.claude/skills/code-review/** linguist-vendored
/package-lock.json linguist-generated
